"status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Inongo town, provincial capital of Maï-Ndombe","evidence":"Inongo is the seat of Maï-Ndombe provincial institutions on Lake Maï-Ndombe, with PNC provincial command and FARDC elements; no armed group is reported to hold or regularly operate in the town. The Mobondo militia active since 2022 is centred on Kwamouth territory far to the south-west.","unit":"CD3302-inongo","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[6]}],"sources":{"6":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202606090742.html","title":"«Les Mobondo ne sont jamais partis» - Dans l'ouest, ce groupe qui sévit toujours malgré le discours officiel","publisher":"AllAfrica / RFI","date":"2026-06-09"},"8":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202608180670.html","title":"Le Gouvernement confirme des signaux de paix face au phénomène Mobondo !","publisher":"AllAfrica","date":"2026-08-18"}},"units":{"CD3302-inongo":"Inongo territory (Maï-Ndombe) covers Inongo town, the provincial capital, and the Inongo, Banzow Moke and Ntandembelo secteurs around Lake Maï-Ndombe. No armed group is reported to control any locality: the town is held by the PNC with FARDC elements, and rural villages fall under ordinary state presence (PNC posts) with customary chiefs. The Mobondo (Teke-Yaka) militia remains active in mid-2026 in Kwamouth and neighbouring areas to the south-west, the nearest risk for Ntandembelo, but is not reported inside Inongo territory. Web research was unavailable for this run, so rural assessments rest on default state presence with low confidence."}}